@version 0.01

@h1{Unit Dimension Math Regression}

@p{Cross-unit-family beam deflection (ft span, in/ksi/in^4 section) - must
match the all-consistent-inches control value of 0.983 in, not silently
collapse to 0 the way the pre-dimension-vector unit engine did.}

@eval
L := 20 ft;

@eval
w := 0.5 kip/in;

@eval
E := 29000 ksi;

@eval
I := 758 in^4;

@eval
delta := 5*w*L^4/(384*E*I);

@p{The 0 - f(x) negation idiom (madola has no unary-minus-before-call syntax)
must work on a unit-bearing expression rather than throwing "Cannot subtract
dimensionless value from value with units".}

v(w, x) := 0 - w*x*(L^3 - 2*L*x^2 + x^3)/(24*E*I);

@eval
mid := v(w, 120 in);

@p{math.abs() must preserve the operand's unit rather than silently
returning a bare number (which previously made a same-unit ratio display as
"1/in" instead of cancelling to dimensionless).}

@eval
ratio := math.abs(delta) / (L/360);
